<BaseLayout title="Leather Philosophy & Care | David Dindi" description="Learn about natural leather variation, marks and practical care for David Dindi leather goods.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Leather philosophy</div><span class="eyebrow">Natural materials</span><h1>Leather has a history of its own.</h1><p class="lead">Natural grain, colour variation and visible marks are part of what makes leather different from synthetic, perfectly uniform materials.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container content">
    <h2>Variation is natural</h2>
    <p>Leather colour and texture can vary from hide to hide and between tannery batches. Natural marks, scars, scratches and tick marks may be visible. These characteristics can reflect the animal's life and the natural history of the hide.</p>
    <h2>Not every mark is a defect</h2>
    <p>Some product ranges may use hides with more visible character, while other designs may be cut from more carefully selected areas. The level of variation depends on the material and the specific product. Product photos should represent the item honestly.</p>
    <h2>Care for your leather</h2>
    <ul class="list-clean"><li>Keep leather away from excessive moisture and direct heat.</li><li>Avoid harsh chemicals, solvents and untested cleaning products.</li><li>Ink, oil and dirty-fluid stains may be difficult or impossible to remove.</li><li>Test any care product on a discreet area and follow material-specific instructions.</li><li>Ask us for advice if you are unsure how to treat a mark.</li></ul>
    <h2>Leather and water</h2>
    <p>Do not assume leather is waterproof. If a product uses a water-resistant or waterproof lining, that does not mean the leather exterior is waterproof. Follow the product-specific information supplied with your item.</p>
    <div class="notice"><strong>Before publishing:</strong> confirm that this wording accurately reflects the way each product range is selected and made. This explanation does not remove any rights customers may have when goods have a genuine defect.</div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>